{
  "chapter_id": "CH014",
  "title": "Operating What You Have",
  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "SEC055",
      "title": "Abnormal Faith, Short Prayers",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Ordinary behavior draws no attention. Only those who do abnormal things, who act in a faith that goes beyond the normal, cause people to take notice. Nobody pays attention to normal people doing normal things; it is the abnormal act of faith that marks a person and carries impact.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA207",
            "SRC005338",
            "SRC005340",
            "SRC005342",
            "SRC005346"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC005338",
            "SRC005340",
            "SRC005342",
            "SRC005346"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA207"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000001",
          "provider_handle": "p1"
        },
        {
          "text": "God told me not to pray long prayers when seeking a miracle. He told me to pray a short prayer, and I want us to follow the model of Jesus in this.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA208",
            "SRC005357",
            "SRC005358",
            "SRC005361",
            "SRC005362"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC005357",
            "SRC005358",
            "SRC005361",
            "SRC005362"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA208"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000002",
          "provider_handle": "p2"
        },
        {
          "text": "Often, acting in faith means moving forward without knowing what the outcome will be. You do not know; you just know that you are acting in obedience, and that step of obedience is what is asked of you, nothing more.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA209",
            "SRC005447",
            "SRC005449",
            "SRC005451"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC005447",
            "SRC005449",
            "SRC005451"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA209"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000003",
          "provider_handle": "p3"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is a testimony of a young woman who had been prophesied to live, yet she died and was buried. The Lord told me to go, and before I came back she had already been buried. The grave was opened at that place, decomposed as it was, and a short prayer was prayed over it. She came out alive, sitting up, and this was later recognized and reported in the Tribune newspaper.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA209",
            "EX032",
            "SRC005256",
            "SRC005260",
            "SRC005349",
            "SRC005416",
            "SRC005422"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC005256",
            "SRC005260",
            "SRC005349",
            "SRC005416",
            "SRC005422",
            "SRC005447",
            "SRC005449",
            "SRC005451",
            "SRC005460",
            "SRC005607"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA209"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX032"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [
            "UNC024"
          ],
          "paragraph_id": "P000004",
          "provider_handle": "p4"
        },
        {
          "text": "The same account returns in the telling: they had buried her, the grave was opened, and the sister was found sitting up alive. The names given in this retelling are Reverend John and Brother Samson, and the details repeat closely enough that it is not fully clear whether this is one event told twice or two distinct occurrences.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "EX033",
            "SRC005460",
            "SRC005463",
            "SRC005605",
            "SRC005617",
            "SRC005661"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC005460",
            "SRC005463",
            "SRC005605",
            "SRC005617",
            "SRC005661",
            "SRC005349",
            "SRC005607"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX033"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [
            "UNC024"
          ],
          "paragraph_id": "P000005",
          "provider_handle": "p5"
        },
        {
          "text": "These are not distant stories from the past. A white preacher connected to such an account is still alive and still preaching in Nigeria; anyone can go to the internet and find him there today.",
          "kind": "connective",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "EX034",
            "SRC005677",
            "SRC005683",
            "SRC005684",
            "SRC005686"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC005677",
            "SRC005683",
            "SRC005684",
            "SRC005686"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX034"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000006",
          "provider_handle": "p6"
        },
        {
          "text": "Even in such a moment, doubt can assail the mind. The thought comes, what if it doesn't work, and the brain keeps working against the step being taken. The minister in this account closed his eyes so as not to see the disappointment, should it come, and proceeded anyway.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA210",
            "SRC005648",
            "SRC005649",
            "SRC005657",
            "SRC005659"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC005648",
            "SRC005649",
            "SRC005657",
            "SRC005659"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA210"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000007",
          "provider_handle": "p7"
        },
        {
          "text": "I never preach a doctrine I do not know. Do not be foolish and claim to know everything; God is too great for anyone to know everything about him. But whatever you do know, it must work for you.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA211",
            "SRC005728",
            "SRC005732",
            "SRC005734",
            "SRC005736",
            "SRC005737"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC005728",
            "SRC005732",
            "SRC005734",
            "SRC005736",
            "SRC005737"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA211"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000008",
          "provider_handle": "p8"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA207",
        "IDEA208",
        "IDEA209",
        "IDEA210",
        "IDEA211"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
